<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! engine.wiki.renders ~ wikify a title or a span through the wiki's own engine

Exactly one of `title` (a tiddler) or `text` (a wikitext span); transclusions, macros, widgets and filters resolve as the wiki resolves them. `form` reads text (the default) or html; `type` names a span's content type. `max-bytes` caps the text, and a truncated answer's `next` rides back as `after`. A render fires no action and dispatches no message. `target` visits another lit face's read view. `output` refuses on the seat: the terminal holds the workbench disk grant.

The address stands ''candidate'' until the operator reads the landing's list. The MCP seat runs this act in its own process: the vessel's `call` binds the params against this carrier's live `#/takes` and answers `handler/seat` with the bound params, and the seat runs them (`act(address="lar:///engine.wiki.renders", args={…})`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ title · text · recipe · form · type · after · max-bytes · target · output

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`title` params=`takes/word ~ the tiddler to render`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`text` params=`takes/word ~ a wikitext span to render`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`recipe` params=`takes/word default/default ~ the wiki (default names the worn face's daemon wiki)`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`form` params=`takes/word ~ text or html`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`type` params=`takes/word ~ a span's content type`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`after` params=`takes/word ~ the cursor a prior page answered as next`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`max-bytes` params=`takes/count ~ the byte cap on the text`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`target` params=`takes/word ~ another lit face to visit (h1, or a pet name)`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`output` params=`takes/word ~ refused on the seat (the terminal holds the workbench grant)`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ seat

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`seat` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ the vessel verbs the seat's handler reaches check the face's cap and the asker's hand themselves; a hand act refuses a seat by its own code`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins`>>

!! skins ~ mcp

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins/mcp`>>

!!! act lar:///engine.wiki.renders

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`skin` name=`mcp` params=`handler/seat spells/[[act lar:///engine.wiki.renders]] ~ the seat runs it in its own process`>>
```

